=== Cones ===

Firs differ from other conifers such as [[spruce]]s in having erect, cylindrical female seed [[Conifer cone|cones]] {{convert|5|-|25|cm|in|0|abbr=on}} long that disintegrate at maturity to release the winged [[seed]]s. Seed cones take a year to become mature; they start out green or other bright colour, darkening as they develop to dark brown or black. The leaflike seed [[bract]]s are visible when young, and in some species remain so. The seeds sit in thin cups; each seed has a triangle-shaped wing. The male cones are pendulous (dangling) and resemble [[catkin]]s; both pollen and seeds are wind-dispersed.<ref name="IDS"/> 

