[[Lucas Cranach the Elder]] painted ''Madonna under the fir tree'' for [[Wrocław Cathedral]] in 1510.<ref>{{cite web |title="Madonna under the Fir Tree" by Lucas Cranach the Elder |date=22 September 2020 |url=https://mnwr.pl/en/madonna/ |access-date=9 September 2025 |publisher=[[National Museum in Wrocław]]}}</ref> The painting was taken to Germany after the Second World War for restoration, but a copy was made and substituted for the original. The forgery was discovered, partly because the copy was on a fir board where the original was on [[Tilia|lime]] wood. The original was returned to Poland in 2012, the most valuable painting to be restituted to the country.<ref>{{cite web |title=Madonna under the Fir Tree |website=The Marian Temples Trail |url=https://maryjny.org/en/zdjecie/madonna-under-the-fir-tree/ |access-date=9 September 2025}}</ref>

